title: 'statement-store: add event-fed v2 peer topology'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    ## Summary

    This PR adds the initial **statement-store v2 peer topology scaffold** for #11933.

    The statement handler now feeds a new `PeersTopology` module from the statement-protocol events it already observes:

    - statement notification substream open/close events;
    - statement-protocol version support for connected peers;

    The topology keeps a local, event-fed view of statement-capable peers and exposes helpers for:

    - tracking seen peers;
    - tracking statement protocol support
    - tracking statement notification connection state;
    - deriving local DHT affinity over the event-fed peer set;
    - selecting closest connected routing targets;

    ## Design notes

    This is intentionally a **topology scaffold**, not the complete statement-store v2 routing/storage implementation.

    `PeersTopology` computes closest peers over the locally learned peer set. It does not issue topic-specific Kademlia lookups and does not yet make statement storage/routing decisions end-to-end.

    The local node is always considered DHT-eligible in this scaffold, so the topology constructor does not expose a separate local eligibility flag.
crates:
- name: sc-network
  bump: patch
- name: sc-network-statement
  bump: patch
